I thought I'd let some of my ridiculous ideas for nethack armor see
the light of day. Here goes:


1. Armor of the berserker, i.e. "super mithril"

AC -7, weight 150. Autocurses because it literally fuses with your
characters' skin.

The ultimate creation of the dwarves, forged of mithril. One suit of
it exists in the masterforge of the dwarves, found in a single magic
portal somewhere in the mines, home to pools of lava, devious traps,
and Durin's Bane - a gigantic Balrog. Hey, at least balrogs are slower
than the possible minotaur at mines' end. There's a 60% chance of
creating it by overenchanting Mithril (either kind), too. *NOT*
randomly generated.

Allows the user to surpass the natural limits set by their body. 50
(or perhaps level * 4) extra HP and +5 to STR and CON in exchange for
a lower healing rate. Eliminates all spellcasting.

(inspired by reading the Berserk manga)

2. Fencing helmet. Half damage from bladed attacks and AC 2.

3. Helm of forgetfulness. Gives a 50% chance neighboring spellcasters
forget their magic words. Provides major spellcasting penalty for
obvious reasons.

4. Tutu. 1/3 chance that intelligent monsters stop to laugh at your
ridiculous outfit. -4 damage penalty. Shirt slot.

5. A dragon toenail. :)

Can be dropped by dragons upon their demise. Acts like a dagger. Does
d5 elemental damage in the case of red, blue, green, or white dragons.
Can be stacked, so if a silly player wants to kill countless dragons
just to get a badass [q]uivered weapon, he can.

6. Gauntlets of nose picking: allow you to regain 2 HP by picking your
nose when [a]pplied. Often cursed. -5 to charisma. Probably the most
frivolous YANI ever. And maybe...

"Picking your nose with a cockatrice corpse is a fatal (and
disgusting) mistake."

You know, really, I just want some player to ascend wearing Gauntlets
of Nose Picking and a tutu, and wielding a dragon toenail.

7. Shield of repulsion: Repels physical attacks, causing d5 passive
damage to target, sort of like the new Sporkhack effect for green
dragon scale mail.

8. Gauntlets of whirlwind:

Blue gloves imbued with the nature of air elementals that posess
blades with their swirling force. Bladed attacks create vortices that
deal 25% damage to any nearby target. Avoid using near peacefuls. :)

9. Silver chain mail:

weight 300, MC3, AC5

Deals passive silver damage to attackers.



